# FlintTrade — data

> Real-time tick capture, WebSocket storage, local audit trails, order flow analysis, tax reports and Practice sandbox storage.

## Key Modules

Modules below live in `src/flinttrade_data/`.

- `tick_recorder.py` — Real-time tick capture and storage
- `audit_logger.py` — Configurable local audit trail retention
- `orderflow.py` / `orderflow_routes.py` — Order flow analysis and API routes
- `tax_report.py` / `tax_routes.py` — Tax report generation and API routes
- `storage.py` — DuckDB storage layer
- `sandbox_engine.py` / `sandbox_routes.py` — Internal Practice execution and API routes

Trade logging and P&L tracking live in `packages/services/journal/src/flinttrade_journal/` (`trade_logger.py`, `pnl_tracker.py`, `journal_routes.py`).

## Absorbs
- openquest → QuestDB tick aggregation, multi-exchange streaming, TradingView charts

## Dependencies

See `packages/core/data/pyproject.toml` for declared dependencies and optional extras.

## Rules
- Read root CLAUDE.md for project-wide rules
- Use `flinttrade_core.openalgo_client` (`packages/core/core/src/flinttrade_core/openalgo_client.py`) for the optional OpenAlgo REST bridge. Live writes must obtain a `SafetyContext` through `gate_order`/`gate_broker_write` and flow through `BrokerRouter`; never call broker writes directly.
- Keep shared service logic broker-neutral; broker-specific implementations and capability differences belong in gateway adapters.
- Tests are in the `tests/` directory. Add new test files as needed.
- Update root `changelog.md` only for shipped user-visible or API changes; do not add entries for tests, behaviour-preserving refactors or in-flight design.
- Branch: follow root AGENTS.md; verify live main before opening or merging a PR.

## Crypto data (Delta Exchange)
- 24/7 tick data — storage grows continuously (no market close)
- Funding rate snapshots every 8 hours
- Liquidation events as separate data stream
- Use CCXT for supplementary crypto data if needed
